\dJust do it.\d%K%P
「好了啦…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dO-Okay...\d%K%P
「哈、哈啊…」%K%P
I did as she asked.%K%P
我一边说着，一边把脸凑到女孩跟前，\n虽然不太情愿，但我也有在意的事。%K%P
I couldn't help but notice how her slightly slanted eyes\nlooked just like Ms. Honoka's.%K%P
大大的丹凤眼稍显失落而垂下…\n她的表情还有她的容貌确实和穗香小姐很像。%K%P
It made me realize that she really was her child.%K%P
啊啊，这孩子，真的是那个人的…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
It all happened on a warm spring day, with cherry blossom\npetals scattering in the wind.%K%P
那是樱花散落，春日的物语。%K%P
Although, in my case, the rose petals scattering in my\nface seemed... a touch more immediate.%K%P
不知为何蔷薇也随之凋零，\n发生在晴朗日子里的事情。%K%P
%LCGirl
%LC女孩
\dYou homewrecker! Give my mother back!\d%K%P
「你这个奸夫！\n把妈妈…把妈妈还给我！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat......?\d%K%P
「诶………………………………………………？」%K%P
Yoshimura Osamu. At twenty-eight years old, on a spring\nday...%K%P
芳村理。二十八岁又十个月，春季的一天。%K%P
That marked the beginning of my life with Hinosaka Mitoko.%K%P
这就是我和她…和阳坂美都子“命运”的缘起…%K%P
As well as the end of my story with Hinosaka Honoka.%K%P
同时也是我和那个人…和阳坂穗香“命运”的终结。%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dLi'l landlord! Li'l landlord!\d%K%P
「房东小妹，房东小妹～！」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIt's open.\d%K%P
「门开着的」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dBig trouble, li'l landlord! There's a dead guy in the\nempty room! Like, socially dead.\d%K%P
「不得了了，房东妹妹！\n本来应该是空房的四号房里有个男人死了！\n主要是在指社会层面上」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dOh... him.\d%K%P
「啊～………是啊」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dYou friends with the stiff?\d%K%P
「你认识啊？\n那具尸体」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWell, if you put it like that... Not really, I guess.\d%K%P
「你要问我认识不认识的话…只能说不算是认识」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dWant me to clean up the mess, then? It'd be a pain to\ncarry someone that big, so I'll cut him to bits.\d%K%P
「那，事不宜迟赶紧给处理了吧？\n整体运出去的话太麻烦了，那就先大卸八块…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI'm sorry, but would you mind letting him stay dead for a\nbit longer? This is partly my fault and everything.\d%K%P
「抱歉…再让他在那多死一会吧。\n我也有些做错了」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dHuh? Hmm, I guess running a place isn't easy.\d%K%P
「啊？呼嗯～，成为经营者后就辛苦起来了啊」%K%P
To Mitoko.%K%P
致美都子。%K%P
It pains my heart to leave while you're still so young. I\ndo not for a moment expect forgiveness.%K%P
抛下年纪轻轻的你这样离去令我无比心酸。\n我并不奢望能得到你的原谅。%K%P
But I have faith that one day, you will come to understand\nmy decision.%K%P
但我相信，总有一天能得到你的理解。%K%P
With that thought to sustain me, I will be able to press\non. I'll grit my teeth and live my life.%K%P
相信着那一天的到来，妈妈也在努力着。\n咬紧牙关，一定能够活下去的。%K%P
(A few pages of excuses and self-justification follow.)%K%P
（这之后，\n絮絮叨叨地写了一大段把自己行为正当化的辩解）%K%P
I met him about three months ago. He found his way to the\nshop I worked at one winter evening.%K%P
妈妈和那个人的相遇大概是在三个月之前…\n在下着大雪的一天，那个人信步来到店里。%K%P
It only took a few words for me to realize he was the one.\nThat it was fate which had brought us together.%K%P
稍稍说了几句话，喝了些酒…仅仅如此，\n我一下子就感到『啊啊，就是这个人了』。\n我们两个的相遇是命运的指引啊。%K%P
(A few pages of sappy boasting follow.)%K%P
（这之后，写了一大段关于男方的痴言梦语）%K%P
I hope one day the two of you can meet. But now is still a\nbit too early.%K%P
我希望有一天美都子你也见见他。\n但现在还不行。%K%P
He's the young leader of a huge organization, and recently\nled a massive project to success. However, due to that, he\nhas become a constant target of headhunting from other\ncorporations.%K%P
他是个大组织的年轻领导人，\n就在前不久刚刚完成了个大项目，但好像也因此\n引来很多同业的公司挖墙脚。%K%P
As such, per the advice of his company, he has decided to\nleave the public eye for the time being.%K%P
所以他和公司的人商量了一下，决定消失一段时间。%K%P
I couldn't let him shoulder this burden alone. You\nunderstand how I feel, don't you?%K%P
不能让他一个人背负如此重的负担…\n美都子你，应该能理解吧？%K%P
I will contact you once things have settled down. Please\nlook after the Terrace House Hinosaka in my absence.%K%P
等过一段时间安定下来了以后，妈妈会联络你。\n在那之前，Terrace House阳之坂就拜托你了。%K%P
I love you more than anyone in the world. Signed, Mom.%K%P
世界上最爱你的妈妈。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...There wasn't even a single mention of me.\d%K%P
「关于我的事…一句话都没提及…」%K%P
There were some similarities in the location and general\ntime frame of our encounters, but...%K%P
相遇的时间和地点，\n的确是和我的情况相似…%K%P
It was plain to see that the man described in this letter\nwasn't me.%K%P
但这里所写的『他』，\n明显不是指我。%K%P
Actually, it felt almost surreal that she was consoling me\nabout my inane daily troubles while simultaneously being\nso madly in love with someone else.%K%P
也就是说，和我相遇，陪我聊天，开导我，\n温柔对待我的同时，\n她自己也被如火的恋情烧灼着。%K%P
In short...%K%P
也就是说…%K%P
It was all in my head. I was the most miserably dense man\nin the world.%K%P
独自一人朝着完全不同方向努力着的我，\n成为了世界上最滑稽且最可悲的第三者。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI want to die... I'd be better off dead... I wish an\nearthquake would just bury me and all my family members\nalive...\d%K%P
「好想死…好想去死…\n在大地震崩塌的溶洞里，全家老小七姑八姨\n全都死光才好…」※译注：出自横沟正史的《八墓村》。%K%P
No matter how many times I re-read the letter, I couldn't\nfind a single word affirming my feelings. To her, I was\nmerely an acquaintance. Nothing more.%K%P
无论读多少遍，回应我情感的内容连一个字都没有提及，\n不如说，我这个存在对她而言，\n只不过是平平常常的聊天对象而已，这个事实沉重地压着我。%K%P
The thought I'd nearly rid myself of during these past\nthree months -- that I wasn't needed in this world --\ngradually crept back into my mind.%K%P
用几个月时间好不容易忘掉的『自我无用论』，\n又开始在心中慢慢萌芽了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI guess... I should've just frozen to death in the snow\nthat day after all... Ugh...\d%K%P
「果然我在那个时候…\n在那个下着大雪的车站前冻死了比较好啊…\n呜、呜呜、呜…」%K%P
Fate was such a convenient word.%K%P
“命运”这个词有时候真是好用…%K%P
A man's life would always be shaped by his own choices,\nnot the whims of some invisible guiding force.%K%P
人的一生，才不是由那种东西决定的。\n万事万物的结局都是自己选择后的必然。%K%P
But sometimes men weren't given the choice to oppose fate\nand change their lives.%K%P
然而，像这样连让自己做出选择的机会都抓不到，\n连冲破命运大门的勇气都觉着有名无实的境遇，\n在这世上比比皆是。%K%P
And at such times, I couldn't help but think that I was\nthe most miserable man in the world.%K%P
那种时候，我们就会这么想——\n啊啊，如今世上没有比我更倒霉的人了吧。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Ah.\d%K%P
「………啊」%K%P
\dGive my mother back!\d%K%P
『把妈妈…把妈妈还给我！』%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
There were those...%K%P
比我还要不幸的人…%K%P
...more miserable than me.%K%P
原来还有啊。%K%P
At this very house.%K%P
我很清楚就在这附近。%K%P
And in a way worse situation to boot.%K%P
而且不幸程度还远远高过我。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm such a...\d%K%P
「我啊…」%K%P
And yet, in spite of how she lashed out at me, she was\nstill considerate enough of my feelings to give me a room\nI could rest in.%K%P
然而，她能在感情一度失控之后…\n了解到我的情况，然后就让我在这里休息了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm such a fool.\d%K%P
「我真是…大笨蛋啊」%K%P
I rolled onto my back and gazed at the ceiling.%K%P
我随便仰躺下来，镶着木板的天花板映入眼帘。%K%P
Had I seen that ancient-looking stain as a child, I'd have\nno doubt imagined it to be the dwelling place of an evil\nspirit.%K%P
无论是谁都会觉得破旧的斑痕，要是小时候的我见了，\n也许会想那上面一定依附着恶灵的真身，\n然后浑身发抖。%K%P
The thin plaster walls surrounding me seemed ready to\ncollapse at any moment, and I doubted the window served\nmuch of a purpose with its frame full of gaps.%K%P
薄薄的石灰墙看起来弱不禁风，\n这木质的窗框感觉完全防不住从间隙里吹进来的风。%K%P
I wondered about Hinosaka Mitoko; how she must have felt,\nbeing left all alone to run a place like this.%K%P
在这栋建筑里，与住户一道被留下的女孩…\n阳坂美都子的辛苦可见一斑…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh...?\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dUm... could you let me in?\d%K%P
「那个…能开下门吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
You could cut the tension between us with a knife.%K%P
气氛好沉重…%K%P
Embarassed about how I'd acted a moment ago, I couldn't\nbring myself to look her in the eye.%K%P
毕竟刚才我那态度，连我自己都感到羞耻不已，\n所以现在还无法直视她的脸。%K%P
A girl likely half my age was holding her own in such a\ntrying situation, while here I was -- a man in his mid-\ntwenties -- wishing myself dead over a silly little\nrejection.%K%P
明明是年纪比我小那么多的女孩子，\n却能如此坚强地面对这种事。\n我这个走到奔三道路中后的大男人反而要死要活的…%K%P
Just remembering it made my face blaze red-hot. I simply\ncouldn't find the words to address her...%K%P
光是想想，脸上好像就要冒出火了。\n而就在嘴边的话语，怎么也说不出…%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...I'm sorry.\d%K%P
「…实在抱歉」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
%XS24\dYes, that's it!\d %XE%K%P
「对，就是这！」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
%XS10\dLook, I'm apologizing, okay? You don't need to shout.\d %XE%K%P
「所以说…人家都在道歉了。\n你就别怒吼了啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAhh! No, that's not what I meant! There was a\ncommunications breakdown!\d%K%P
「啊啊，不对不对！\n重大的交流分歧！」%K%P
It seemed as though the exaggerated theatrics of a quiz\nshow were painfully out of place in this awkward scene.%K%P
『正确！』的这种反应夸张到了能和搞笑节目相提并论，\n但在这阴郁的气氛中似乎没起到什么好作用。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dCommunications... what?\d%K%P
「communication…错误？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, um, in layman's terms, it means that I'm the one who\nshould be apologizing...\d%K%P
「啊，那个，也就是说…按照日常对话的说法，\n就是『应该道歉的人是我』的意思…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhy? You only came looking for my mom, old man.\d%K%P
「为什么？\n叔叔你只不过是来探访妈妈的…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOld man... Old man...\d%K%P
「叔叔…叔叔什么的…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAre you really gonna get hung up on that now?\d%K%P
「就算你这么岔开话题也…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm still in my mid-twenties...\d%K%P
「我…其实也只是二十过半而已啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSo... how old are you, exactly?\d%K%P
「二十…几？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dLike I said, I'm in my mid-twenties.\d%K%P
「不不，所以说是“过半”」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
