%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Twenty-eight.\d%K%P
「………八」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSo, anyway, sorry for flipping out on you, old man. You\njust came to see my mom.\d%K%P
「嗯，叔叔你只不过是来探访妈妈的，\n我却突然做了那种事情…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIs that your idea of a sincere apology?\d%K%P
「你真的有向我道歉的意思吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...Say what?\d%K%P
「…你说啥？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...N-Nothing. Like I said, I'm the one at fault here,\nso...\d%K%P
「…不不，所以说是我不对啦～」%K%P
She could be kind of intimidating...%K%P
好、好可怕…%K%P
Was she really Ms. Honoka's daughter...?%K%P
这孩子，真的是“那个”穗香小姐的女儿…\n没错的吧？%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dBut really, I'm sorry for misunderstanding you. Now that\nI think about it, it wouldn't make any sense for the guy\nMom eloped with to just come here on his own so suddenly.\d%K%P
「没有那种事啦…是我搞错了真的很抱歉。\n话说回来，冷静想想的话，和妈妈私奔的那个人\n是不可能如此恬不知耻地回来这里的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
This again...%K%P
又这样…%K%P
And so, once again, I found myself the one being consoled.%K%P
她又在鼓励我、安慰我了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI guess I lacked composure back there. And that's the\nkind of situation where I should be keeping my cool,\ntoo... Guess I've still got a ways to go, huh?\d%K%P
「稍微欠缺了一些冷静啊。\n明明在这种时候是最应该保持冷静的，\n我真的是还差得远啊…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell...\d%K%P
「那是…」%K%P
That really wasn't something for a girl her age to worry\nabout.%K%P
本来，这个年龄段的女孩子就应该是风风火火的，\n本来就没有必要具备那种思想觉悟的。%K%P
My sorry situation was nothing compared to how she must\nhave felt.%K%P
与不得不做这种不必要反省的她相比，\n我的那点不幸简直还没到人家脚趾豆。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI think we should both try to calm down, okay?\d%K%P
「我们双方都不太冷静啊，是吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYeah.\d%K%P
「是啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHaha...\d%K%P
「哈哈…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAhaha...\d%K%P
「啊哈哈…」%K%P
Well, whatever. This was fine.%K%P
所以，这样就好。%K%P
I believed I was the only one at fault, but it wasn't my\nplace to deny any responsibility she might have been\nfeeling.%K%P
虽然我是觉得这只是我一个人的错，\n但也没有否认这孩子『是自己不对』的想法，\n我是如此思考的。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAnyway, have this as a token of our reconciliation.\d%K%P
「那，这个给你，作为和好的证明…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat's this?\d%K%P
「啥？」%K%P
That tray with a tea towel covering it had actually been\nbothering me for a while now.%K%P
其实我刚才就已经注意到了，那个盖着布巾的盘子。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWell, you see...\d%K%P
「这个啊，是…」%K%P
She began to unwrap the tea towel.%K%P
她用手掀开盖着的布，展现在我面前…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou're hungry, aren't you? You haven't eaten anything\nsince this morning.\d%K%P
「肚子饿了吧？\n从早上到现在你什么都没吃吧？」%K%P
A wrapped plate and a covered bowl rested on the tray.%K%P
那个盘子里，是用保鲜膜盖住的食碟\n和盖着盖子的碗。%K%P
I removed the plastic wrap to find three rice balls and\ntwo slices of pickled daikon. Inside the bowl, there was\nsteaming miso soup.%K%P
掀开保鲜膜，里面是三个饭团和两片腌萝卜。\n揭开碗的盖子，味噌汤的香味立刻弥散开来。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThis one has salmon, then this here is skipjack tuna, and\nfinally, we have pickled plum. I used seaweed, tofu, and\ndaikon for the miso soup.\d%K%P
「从这边开始，是鲑鱼馅，干鲣鱼，梅干。\n味噌汤的用料是裙带菜和豆腐还有萝卜」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dGo on... Help yourself before it gets cold.\d%K%P
「请用。\n趁热吃吧…？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
She exuded an almost palpable sincerity, her heart tender\nand clear like a crystal.%K%P
这一刻，我好像看到了少女那澄澈通透的心灵，\n没有任何虚假、暖暖的真情实意。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhat's wrong? I didn't add anything weird, if that's what\nyou're worried about.\d%K%P
「怎么了？\n完全没有加任何奇怪的东西进去哦？」%K%P
As such, I had to answer her in kind.%K%P
所以我也…\n必须像她那样，毫无虚假、诚实地回应她。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dY-Yeah... I'm not worried about that.\d%K%P
「唔，嗯…这一点我明白，不过…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThen what's wrong?\d%K%P
「不过、什么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dTo tell the truth, I...\d%K%P
「其实…那个…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dGod, you're beating around the bush again. Just come out\nand say it.\d%K%P
「真是的，又在那磨磨蹭蹭的。\n有什么话就爽快地说出来啊，大叔」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dTo tell you the truth, I can't eat rice. Ah, it's not an\nallergy or anything. But I'd prefer either bread or\nsome--\d%K%P
「其实我啊…平时不吃米蒸的饭的。\n不不，我并不是过敏。\n不过，面包的话我还是吃的…」%K%P
.........%K%P
………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI want to die... I'd be better off dead...\d%K%P
「好想死…好想去死…」%K%P
......%K%P
……%K%P
...%K%P
…%K%P
%LCElderly Man
%LC上年纪的男人
\dWell, you're in the wrong there, no matter how one looks\nat it. I don't know of anyone who'd refuse such an obvious\ngesture of kindness just because the food is not to their\ntaste.\d%K%P
「不不，是你的问题。就算你再怎么不爱吃米饭，\n但那毕竟是人家好不容易给你做的，\n哪有人会白痴到直接说我不爱吃的啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dB-But I really can't stand rice. The smell is enough to\nget me completely...\d%K%P
「可、可是…我是真的完全吃不了米饭。\n光是闻到那个味道都…」%K%P
%LCElderly Man
%LC上年纪的男人
\dYou could have at least come up with a proper way to\nrefuse. Like, 'Ah, my family was obsessed with rice balls;\nwe ate them in heaps, sometimes shoving more than one into\nour mouths.%K%P
「就算这样，你也不能直接拒绝人家啊。那种情况下，\n你应该说『啊，真令人高兴。我家里人经常一起吃这个饭团子，\n眼都不眨，吃了一个、两个，回过神来吃了三个、四个……%K%P
\d'But one day, my father ate so many he choked and passed\naway. Since that fateful day, I've been unable to stomach\nrice balls.'\d%K%P
可是有一天，我父亲吃得太多，噎住之后就去世了。自从那不幸的一天起，我就再也吃不下饭团子了。」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Hahh.\d%K%P
「………哈啊」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dYo, Mr. Retired. You're rambling again.\d%K%P
「喂、喂，老爷子老爷子。别扯远了」%K%P
%LCMuscular Man
%LC肌肉男
\dSorry. He's been like that ever since he tried working as\nan advisor to a rakugo club.\d%K%P
「抱歉啊，自打成为了落语研究会的顾问，\n他就变得越来越啰嗦了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI... I see.\d%K%P
「哈、哈啊」%K%P
The elderly man sitting in front of me wearing the haori\nwas the tenant of Room #1, Uesaka Kihee.%K%P
正坐于我对面，整整齐齐地穿着短褂子的老男人\n是一号房间的住户，名字好像叫上坂喜兵卫。%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dI hear he was a professor at some university or other.\d%K%P
「他以前好像是某所大学里很牛的教授」%K%P
%LCMuscular Man
%LC肌肉男
\dBut then they found out he planted some false stoneware\nwith a small mirror at one of his excavation sites so he\ncould look up the girls' skirts.\d%K%P
「不过有一次他把一个伪造成石器的小镜子偷偷带进了发掘现场，\n用它偷看女孩裙底的时候被人发现了…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI... I see?\d%K%P
「哈、哈啊？」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dHey now, think when you speak. You're confusing the\nprofessor with the assistant.\d%K%P
「喂喂，别胡乱说些凭空臆造的东西。\n你这不是把教授和助教搞混了吗」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOh, so that's the only problem you found with that...\d%K%P
「在那胡乱说些凭空臆造东西的人不就是你么…」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dAnyway, so what -can- ya eat if rice is no good, bro?\d%K%P
「那，小哥你不吃米饭平时都吃什么啊？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, um... spaghetti, pizza, and other kinds of Western\nfood, I suppose.\d%K%P
「啊，那个…像是通心粉啊，披萨之类的啦，那些西餐」%K%P
...Did he just call me a bro?%K%P
…小哥？%K%P
It wasn't until middle school that I learned I couldn't\neat certain things.%K%P
知道有自己不爱吃的东西，\n还是在我上初中的时候。%K%P
Up until then, I wasn't even aware of the existence of\nJapanese cuisine. I guess I was raised in a pretty unusual\nhousehold.%K%P
在那之前，就连日式饭菜的存在\n没准我都没有认识到。\n毕竟我就在那种家庭里长大的。%K%P
My first fated encounter with rice could be attributed to\na housekeeper whose face I no longer remember.%K%P
然后，第一次吃到的米饭，\n是一位我已经记不得长什么样的女佣做的。%K%P
...The festering, gooey mass got stuck in my throat, and I\nended up vomiting for the rest of the day.%K%P
…黏黏糊糊的饭粒仿佛馊了一般，缠在喉咙里，\n我吐了出来之后，又吐了好久。%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dA housekeeper?! Guys, we've got a rich kid over here!\d%K%P
「女佣！？这小哥是个少爷啊！？」%K%P
%LCMuscular Man
%LC肌肉男
\dWell, he must have been well-fed to grow that tall. Guess\nhe's never seen a lick of trouble his entire life.\d%K%P
「确实，身子板弱不禁风跟个竹竿似的呐。\n是不是因为从小到大就没吃过什么苦啊？」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dRight, it's been decided. Starting today, we'll call you\nYoung Master. Suits you perfectly, don't it?\d%K%P
「好，就这样吧。\n从今天开始就叫你小少爷了。\n怎么样，正合适吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dN-No, it wasn't like that. My parents were just busy...\d%K%P
「不、不不，我家不是什么名门大户啦…\n只是我的双亲俩人都很忙而已」%K%P
And they weren't on the best of terms, either.%K%P
追加一提，那俩人关系也很不好。%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dWell, when it comes to the battle between Western and\nJapanese cuisine, Chinese always ends up as the victor,\nanyway. Oh, I'm going riichi.\d%K%P
「嘛，日式和西式的争端就以中餐作结吧。\n哎呀，我这里可是要立直了哦？」\n※译注：立直，日麻里门清明听的说法，一番。%K%P
Now that I thought about it...%K%P
现在想想…%K%P
I may not have had financial troubles growing up, but\nemotional support? That was an entirely different story.%K%P
在金钱方面是否曾经富裕过先不说，\n要说在心灵层面上有没有过上充实的生活，\n我是完全没有点头的自信。%K%P
Maybe that's why I kept failing when it came to matters of\nthe heart.%K%P
没准就是因为这一点，\n我才总是在追求爱的道路上被命运捉弄。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHahh...\d%K%P
「哈啊…」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dOh, Young Master, it seems I got a hand on my first go.\nMentanpin ippatsu ippeikou. I'll be taking those points\noff your hands.\d%K%P
「哎呀，小少爷，你点了一发喽。\n门断平一发一杯口，亲满贯的说呦？」\n※译注：门清立直断幺平胡一发一杯口，5番记庄满贯1W2K点。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Eh?\d%K%P
「…诶？」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dI see... so you took full responsibility for your\ncompany's fraud... That was pretty stupid of you.\d%K%P
「原来是这样…\n公司不正当经营的责任全被推到自己身上了…\n你真是蠢啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, I had no choice at the time. The entire corporation\nmight have been done for otherwise.\d%K%P
「不不，那个时候是真的没办法了。\n不那样做的话，公司就会面临生存危机了啊」%K%P
What I did was not misguided.%K%P
没错，至少我做的并不是件错事。%K%P
If I hadn't destroyed all the evidence with the director's\nsignatures, it wouldn't have been just me roaming the\nstreets in search of a new job, but hundreds of others.%K%P
那个时候，要是不把盖着董事长大印的审批文件处理掉的话，\n现在到处乱窜找工作求职的人恐怕会不下于三位数了。%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dSo, Laid-off. Lemme tell you somethin' good.\d%K%P
「我说，失业的。告诉你一件有意思的事吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI-I don't think you're in a position to call me that...\d%K%P
「哪、哪有像你这么称呼人的…」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dDon't be that way... I thought we were close.\d%K%P
「别那么说嘛…\n我不是失业先生的朋友吗」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dIf you don't want to be called Laid-off, then how about\nyou find a job and pay your dues to society, hm?\d%K%P
「再说，你要真不想被人叫做失业的，\n那就好好找个工作去给社会做贡献去啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHHHH!!\d%K%P
「………唔哇啊啊啊啊啊啊！？」%K%P
%LCMuscular Man
%LC肌肉男
\d...Creepy, ain't it? I still can't get used to it\nmyself.\d%K%P
「…够瘆人的吧？\n我到现在都还没习惯呢」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dHattsuan's a genius when it comes to acting out voices.\d%K%P
「小八他啊…\n在发音方面是个天才级别的演员哦」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dActing out...?\d%K%P
「演员…？」%K%P
%LCMuscular Man
%LC肌肉男
\dHe joined some troupe instead of attending classes at his\nuniversity. He's both acting and writing scripts, but I\nhear he keeps getting in trouble over women.\d%K%P
「大学也不去，就天天泡在剧团里，\n做演员啦写剧本啦，什么都干。\n毕竟他在男女关系上很不检点」%K%P
%LCYoung Man
%LC年轻男子
\dWhat kind of explanation is that? Half of those things\ndon't even connect.\d%K%P
「不，这话作为说明是不成立的」%K%P
What was up with the people in this place?%K%P
这里的住户都是些什么人啊…%K%P
To my right sat the master of this room, Yasunaga\nBuntarou, a first year student at some university -- three\nyears in a row now, apparently. He was sipping beer\nthrough a straw in almost nirvanic peace.%K%P
在我右边靠着墙用吸管嘬着啤酒的是\n这公寓二号室的房客，八须永文太郎君。\n这是他读大学的第三个年头，但好像还在念大一来着…？%K%P
So we had a former professor and rakugo aficionado, plus\nan actor who had a genius-like talent for doing voices.\nThis was quite the artistic boarding house.%K%P
不过话说回来，原大学教授的单口相声专家，\n能任意改变声线的剧团演员，\n这里真是栋充满了艺术氛围的公寓啊。%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dSo anyway, Mr. Laid-off...\d%K%P
「嘛，那些都先放一边，失业的…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dLook, it wasn't like that, okay? I was just fired because\nof fraud charges.\d%K%P
「所以说了我不是什么失业者，\n只是因为违规被发现而遭到解雇了而已…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dWell, that sounds even worse than bein' downsized. I\nmean, that's quite a recommendation -- the guy who\nbetrayed the company. How're you gonna get another job\nnow? I doubt they hand out golden parachutes with those.\d%K%P
「那样的话可是会遭到比失业还要残酷的待遇啊。\n再就业的话不仅得不到什么优待，\n而且本来应该拿到的退休金也变成了背叛者的称号了呐」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUh...\d%K%P
「唔…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dYou can gloat over saving the company all you want, but\nyou're just a rabbit deluding himself, thinking he was\nbeing helpful to the wolf. It's anger, discontent, and\nlust that makes life worth living, not that other crap.\d%K%P
「我拯救了公司之类的，这样的自我满足是最幼稚的幻想。\n能吃到像鲷○鱼君那样鲜嫩多汁的就好了。生活正是\n因为愤怒和不满以及性欲的爆发才会闪耀的哦」\n※译注：出自子门真人的《游吧！ 鲷鱼君》。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI-I beg to differ, personally. If my actions brought a\nsmile to the face of at least one person, a little snippet\nof their happiness makes my life happier too, don't you\nthink?\d%K%P
「我、我可不那么想。\n自己所做的一切能让笑出来的人哪怕只多一个，\n自己也多少也会分享到一点他们的幸福，你不这么认为吗？」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dWell, I don't doubt the crooks you saved are smiling ear\nto ear right now.\d%K%P
「那倒是，被你所救的那些大佬们现在大概\n正坐在他们的宝座上哈哈大笑着吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThose tears the president shed in front of me were\ngenuine. I believe that.\d%K%P
「我啊，相信那时候部长流出来的眼泪是真心的」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dThen how about you celebrate our landlord's new elopement\nventure? If those two are smiling, then a part of their\nhappiness makes your life happier too, no?\d%K%P
「那你也顺道祝福一下房东小姐的私奔呗。\n逃走的两位要是笑得很开心的话，失业小哥你多少\n也能从中分享到点幸福吧？」%K%P
